# Every job below is wrapped in scripts/cron_job.py. Two jobs on this box died
# silently for months (autoheal stopped 2026-07-29; media_ops_status.py's line
# had no `cd`, so the ops dashboard served June data until September). The
# wrapper pushes an ntfy alert on a fatal exit AND records logs/cron-state/<job>.json
# so stack_watchdog.py can alert when a job simply stops running -- the half that
# produces no output to notice. --max-age-min is how long that job may go without
# succeeding; --ok-codes defaults to 0,1 because this repo's scripts use
# 0 success / 1 partial / 2 fatal and several report findings as 1.
# The wrapper goes INSIDE flock: `flock -n` exits 1 without running anything when
# the lock is held, which outside the wrapper would look like a successful run.
# EVERY line must `cd /home/tom/nas` before any relative path -- cron's $HOME is
# /home/tom and there is no .venv there. That is the bug that cost three months.

# NAS stack — operations crontab
# All entries cd into /home/tom/nas first so the local venv + relative log
# paths resolve. Cleanup scripts share /tmp/nas-tubifarry-cleanup.lock to
# prevent overlapping runs.

